From dedb610380a3763130f154832148de8640adcfb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LOOP ... WHERE over a sorted primary key: binary-search the
 block

A LOOP AT itab WHERE narrowed by binary search only on a secondary key.
Over a SORTED primary key it evaluated the WHERE on every row, also when
topEquals says the first key field has to equal a value - then the rows
the WHERE can accept are one contiguous block. abap2UI5's JSON serializer
(z2ui5_cl_ajson, a fork of abapGit's ajson) does such a LOOP once per
node over its node table, so a model of n nodes cost n^2: the event
roundtrip of a 2000-row table took 22.6 s in a CAP project, 1.8 s with
this change (and the CP change beside it).

The loop now binary-searches the first row that does not sort before the
value and stops at the first row that sorts after it - not at the first
row that is merely unequal, because INSERT LINES OF into the table in the
body re-sorts it without moving the loop index. Only for operands whose
order agrees with the table's sort: the key field's own type (and length
for c, n, x), or a c operand against a string field. Everything else
scans as before. Relies on topEquals holding only conditions every row
has to meet, which the transpiler emits for a pure conjunction since the
previous commit.

Also carries two fixes the narrowing runs into: determineFromTo starts
1-based when topEquals lacks the key's field (the loop started at index
-1), and the loop never reads array[array.length] after a DELETE in the
body.
